    ":question/problem": "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $2$nd and $4$th rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $2$nd and $4$th rows of  $A$ are $1$ and $3$, respectively.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, the answer is $1+3=4.$"
