    ":question/math-academy-id": "q-73145",
    ":question/problem": "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $1$st and $4$th rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $1$st and $4$th rows of $A$ are $1$ and $-3$, respectively.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the answer is $1+(-3)=-2.$"
